To confirm that TBK1 activation during mitosis was dependent on NAP1, we generated two independent NAP1 CRISPR knockout (KO) clones targeting exon 4 (
Fig. 2 A
). Both NAP1 KO HeLa clones displayed decreased p-TBK1 levels during mitosis (
Fig. 2, A and B
). This result was specific to NAP1 because p-TBK1 levels were restored during mitosis upon stable reintroduction of the protein (
Fig. 2, C and D
).
